# LINE Business OS Is One Platform

LINE Business OS is a **single multi-tenant SaaS platform** for Japanese SMBs.
All products (Workforce, Booking, Logistics, CRM, Inventory, AI) are **modules**
that run inside one shared Core — never standalone apps.

## Scale target and current infrastructure

- 🎯 The platform is designed to eventually serve **300+ client tenants** on
  shared multi-tenant infrastructure.
- 💸 At the **current stage, keep infrastructure minimal and free where
  possible** — do not provision paid/dedicated infra ahead of real demand.
- 🧱 Use **one repo, one Vercel project, and one Supabase/PostgreSQL database**
  at this stage. Scale via multi-tenancy (`tenant_id` + RLS), not by spinning up
  per-client repos, projects, or databases.
- 💳 Paid tiers (Founder, 2026-10-17): Vercel Pro from the first paying client
  (Hobby is non-commercial only), Supabase Pro after the first 5. Never rely on
  free-tier-only behaviour; the switch must be a settings change.
- 📡 No polling for live data: push via Supabase Realtime change signals
  (0127, `docs/architecture/realtime-live-updates.md`); timers only through
  `useVisiblePolling` as a slow safety net. Every PR adding a screen, job or
  live table states its per-tenant cost (server calls, Realtime messages,
  storage). See AGENTS.md "Scale and cost".

## Do not create isolated projects

- ❌ Do NOT scaffold a separate repo/app for Workforce, Booking, demo, or
  client-template.
- ❌ Do NOT duplicate Core (auth, tenant context, RBAC, audit, db client) per
  module.
- ✅ Add new product code as a package/module that depends on `@line-os/core`,
  `@line-os/db`, etc.

## Demo and client-template are tenants, not codebases

Demo and client-template differ only by `tenant.kind`, `settings`, and seed
data. Never fork the codebase to create them.

## Layout

```
apps/web (Next.js) · apps/api (NestJS) · apps/worker (jobs/reminders)
packages/core|db|line|ai|ui|config|workforce|booking
supabase/migrations|seed · docs/
```

## Before implementing a module feature

Check `docs/architecture`, the `tenant_id` requirement, RLS impact, RBAC
(`packages/core/src/permissions.ts`), audit requirement, and cross-module
impact — then run lint/build/tests.
